  "maturePack": {
        "notes": "The optional Mature packs (docs/LOCAL_AI.md, 'Mature content'; packaging/MATURE_PACK_README.md): two optional downloads, Mature lite and Mature standard, each ONE zip holding one uncensored model file (lite and good like the Local AI packs) and its own marker (manifest.mature-lite.json, manifest.mature-standard.json) that the main mod reads to say in the setting's help whether a Mature model is installed and to offer it in the Local AI model row (turning Mature content on selects the good one if it fits, else the lite one); each works alone, and the Mature content setting itself is part of the main mod and works without the packs. They are distributed ONLY as files on the project's Hugging Face repository (alystria-ai/ai-npc-cyberpunk-mod-packs, one folder per version; packaging/upload-packs.py), never on Nexus Mods and not on the GitHub release (packaging/MATURE_PACK_RELEASE_NOTES.md has the text for the Hugging Face page). The release workflow builds and uploads them only when its opt-in 'mature' input is set (never on a tag push), one matrix job per pack; by hand they are built with --packages mature-lite or mature-standard. They are never part of the default set, and nothing of them is in the Runtime package. Both models are pinned by revision, size and SHA-256 from the Hugging Face file listing (2026-10-14; both downloaded, SHA-256 checked and run in docs/MATURE_SAMPLES_V3_2026-10-14.md); 'remote' is the file's path inside the repository when it is in a folder. They were chosen from the community data in docs/MATURE_MODELS_V2_2026-10-14.md and confirmed with scripts/Eval-MatureSamples.mjs (third round: docs/MATURE_SAMPLES_V3_2026-10-14.md).",
    "status": "pinned",
    "mirror": {"bucket": "mature/", "manifest": "mature/MANIFEST.json", "notes": "Copies of the two model files in the private bucket (outside final/, so the trained-model fetch never downloads them), so a takedown of the community repositories cannot break a build. --models hf takes each model from here (SHA-256 checked against the pins above) and falls back to the pinned public URL when the mirror lacks it."},
    "markers": {"lite": "manifest.mature-lite.json", "good": "manifest.mature-standard.json"},
    "directory": "mature",
